            <ArticleTitle>Studies of psychosocial influences on coronary artery atherogenesis in cynomolgus monkeys.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>113-24</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The cynomolgus macaque provides a suitable primate model for studying how psychosocial factors contribute to coronary artery atherogenesis. Important interactions with diet, sex, and behaviorally elicited cardiovascular reactivity are described.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
